{
 "schemaVersion": 1,
 "id": "kukhnya-s01e18-scene-17",
 "pair": "ru-en",
 "title": "Увольнения  (Firings)",
 "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
 "labels": {
  "barinov": "Шеф",
  "nagiyev": "Нагиев"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Kristina's plans for the budget have landed on Nagiyev's desk, and he has decided to dismiss the highest-paid cooks. Barinov hears about it, and the two have a furious argument in the office. Listen for the moment Barinov plays his last card.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Я должен уволить твоих поваров.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ты совсем сошёл с ума?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Они слишком дорого стоят.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Это почти полмиллиона каждый месяц.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ты не можешь их увольнять.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Это лучшая команда в Москве.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Дешевле найти новых людей.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Какая разница, кто режет морковь?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Это моя команда!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Если ты их уволишь, ты потеряешь меня.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Витя, просто сядь и успокойся.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Хорошо, разбирайтесь сами.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "А я пока увольняюсь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Подожди, мы всё решим.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Now the row, one blow at a time.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Я должен уволить твоих поваров.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I have to fire your cooks.' \"Povar\", cook, becomes \"povarov\": people on the receiving end of a plural action take that ending.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ты совсем сошёл с ума?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Have you gone completely mad?' \"Soyti s uma\" is 'to go off your mind'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Они слишком дорого стоят.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'They cost too much.' \"Stoyat\", cost, is stressed on the first syllable; with the stress at the end, \"stoyat\" means they stand.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Это почти полмиллиона каждый месяц.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'That's nearly half a million every month.' \"Pol-\", half, is glued on: \"polmilliona\", like \"polchasa\", half an hour.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ты не можешь их увольнять.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You can't fire them.' Barinov picks \"uvolnyat\", the ongoing partner of \"uvolit\": that's the usual choice when something is ruled out.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Это лучшая команда в Москве.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'It's the best team in Moscow.' \"Luchshaya\", the best, agrees with feminine \"komanda\". After \"v\", \"Moskva\" becomes \"Moskve\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Дешевле найти новых людей.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'It's cheaper to find new people.' \"Deshevle\", cheaper, from \"deshevo\", cheap. \"Lyudi\", people, becomes \"lyudey\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Какая разница, кто режет морковь?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'What difference does it make who chops carrots?' \"Kakaya raznitsa\" is the everyday 'who cares'. \"Morkov\" covers one carrot or a pile of them.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Это моя команда!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'It's my team!' \"Komanda\" means a team, and also an order, a command.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Если ты их уволишь, ты потеряешь меня.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'If you fire them, you'll lose me.' Russian puts both halves in the future: 'if you will fire them', \"uvolish\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Витя, просто сядь и успокойся.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Just sit down and calm down.' \"Syad\", sit down!, and \"uspokoysya\", calm yourself, with \"-sya\" on the end.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Хорошо, разбирайтесь сами.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'All right, sort it out yourselves.' \"Razbiraytes\" speaks to more than one person. \"Sami\", yourselves.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "А я пока увольняюсь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And meanwhile I'm quitting.' \"Uvolnyayus\" is 'I fire myself'. \"Poka\", meanwhile, is the same word as the casual bye.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Подожди, мы всё решим.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Wait, we'll sort it all out.' \"Podozhdi\", wait!, is friendly. \"Reshim\", we'll decide, promises a result. Now the whole row, as it happened.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Я должен уволить твоих поваров.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ты совсем сошёл с ума?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Они слишком дорого стоят.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nagiyev",
   "t": "Это почти полмиллиона каждый месяц.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ты не можешь их увольнять.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
